WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.550
- [Kelly] Have a seat!

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:02.770
- Hi guys!

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.175
- [Kelly] Hi! Oh I like your shoes!

00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:05.400
- Oh, thank you very much.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.700
I try and be fashion forward.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.570
- [Kelly] Those are Nikes? Those are cool!

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:09.403
I've never seen those.

00:00:09.403 --> 00:00:11.870
- [Jamie] Well now see
I'm middle-aged now,

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.160
I've got five kids.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.870
I used to be young. It was great Hailee.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:15.970
- [Kelly] I'm 39. I'm middle,

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:16.803
Is that middle aged? Right?

00:00:16.803 --> 00:00:18.210
- I'm 46, you know?

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.043
- [Kelly] Oh? Who cares?

00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:19.945
- But I'm still, I'm still going!

00:00:19.945 --> 00:00:21.070
- [Kelly] Yeah! You're, you're getting,

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.220
You're getting your closing
on Harry Potter, dude.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.273
You're killing it! (laughs)

00:00:25.273 --> 00:00:26.260
- Yep.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.093
- [Kelly] Well meet Hailee.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.986
She just, she just started
loving baking by the way.

00:00:28.986 --> 00:00:30.410
- Thank you.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.500
- So you live in the UK.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.140
So is coming here like your first trip

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:33.973
since like Covid?

00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:34.910
- [Jamie] I'm so excited to be back.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:35.743
- [Kelly] Oh good!

00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:36.940
- And I've been blessed.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.300
I never thought I'd be able to work in

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.140
another country or America.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.910
So I used to come over a
couple of times a year.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.000
Love it!

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.080
Love the variation of cities,
and the food, and the culture.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.784
But yeah, two years of going nowhere.

00:00:48.784 --> 00:00:49.617
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:50.670
- So I'm literally biting to get out.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.990
So yeah, it's good!

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:52.823
- Biting to get out.

00:00:52.823 --> 00:00:53.950
You're a chef. That's clever.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:54.783
- Absolutely!
(audience laughs)

00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:55.616
- [Kelly] So you have,

00:00:55.616 --> 00:00:57.030
you have a beautiful family.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.160
And we both have kids named River.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.400
Yours is a son, right?
- Yes!

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.290
- [Kelly] Yeah, mine's a girl.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.123
- Yeah.

00:01:02.123 --> 00:01:03.346
- [Kelly] What are your other kid's names?

00:01:03.346 --> 00:01:05.150
Oh my gosh!

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:05.983
- [Jamie] Yeah, he's very cute.

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:07.670
- [Kelly] Adorable pumpkin patch alert.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.503
- Don't fall for it.

00:01:08.503 --> 00:01:10.810
He's like, he gives me the
most grief when I cook food.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:11.643
- [Hailee] Oh no!

00:01:11.643 --> 00:01:12.476
- [Kelly] So does my River.

00:01:12.476 --> 00:01:14.423
- He just says "I hate
it! I hate it! Ahh!"

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.810
And then when he puts it in his mouth,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.930
then he sort of comes around.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:18.920
But it's like,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.410
a five-year-old shouldn't
make me feel so bad.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.310
But then, but then he builds me up.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.420
Anyway, so anyway, I've got five kids,

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.690
Poppy, Daisy, Petal,

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:29.680
and then Buddy,

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.660
and then that's River.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.620
So they're all quite floral.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.417
- [Kelly] Yeah, I was gonna
say, someone's into flowers.

00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:36.670
- And that's my wife that
makes up all the names.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.950
I have no, nothing to do with it.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:39.830
I get told at the end.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.090
Actually the papers
normally find out before I

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.650
know what my children's names are.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.780
- But you're the, you
just said the first names.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.087
I have seen your children's names.

00:01:47.087 --> 00:01:48.460
- [Jamie] Well, you're
gonna have to quote it,

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.293
'cause I can't even remember.

00:01:49.293 --> 00:01:51.230
- [Kelly] No, I'm just
saying your kid's, no they're

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.330
they're full on.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:55.980
I am interested to know if
your wife likes weed. (laughs)

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.606
- Yeah. No, no.

00:01:57.606 --> 00:02:00.000
- [Kelly] Because when
I read your kids' names,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.100
I was like, this chick,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.250
she was, she got real
high and she was like,

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.520
this is an amazing name.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.100
Like they're great!

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.160
They're so thought out!

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:08.993
- I can remember River's.

00:02:08.993 --> 00:02:12.210
So it's River Rocket Dallas Blue Oliver.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.280
- [Hailee] That's his? That's one name.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.128
That's one person?

00:02:14.128 --> 00:02:14.961
- [Kelly] No that's what I'm saying!

00:02:14.961 --> 00:02:15.833
- [Jamie] Look, I don't know!

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:16.820
I just married her!

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.370
I have nothing to, I can't.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.340
- It's amazing!

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.526
I want to hang out with
her, from these names alone.

00:02:20.526 --> 00:02:21.990
- [Hailee] Wait, can you
say it one more time?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.354
- River Rocket Dallas Blue Oliver.

00:02:24.354 --> 00:02:25.187
- [Hailee] River Rocket Dallas Blue.

00:02:25.187 --> 00:02:26.080
- [Kelly] Yeah, well I like
the Dallas 'cause I'm Texan.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.620
- But I think my wife has got a thing

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.863
about American Cowboys.

00:02:30.863 --> 00:02:31.696
- [Kelly] Yeah!
(audience cheers)

00:02:31.696 --> 00:02:32.750
- And many years ago, yeah!

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.730
Yeah, well clearly.
- (Kelly laughs)

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.150
- I filmed in Arizona a while
back and I was able to get

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.480
kitted out properly and
I sent her a picture.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.900
And I think it's the only
time I had a really good,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.980
naughty email back saying, "mhmm!"

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.598
- Ah, yeah! (laughs)

00:02:51.598 --> 00:02:52.465
- Number six!

00:02:52.465 --> 00:02:54.140
- [Kelly] (laughs) I love it!
- [Hailee] Oh my God.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.290
- Anyway, I had the chaps and everything,

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.123
I went and full home.

00:02:57.123 --> 00:03:01.030
Chaps, boots, the little
dinkely things that spin.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:01.863
- Spurs.

00:03:01.863 --> 00:03:02.696
- Which I use as,

00:03:02.696 --> 00:03:03.529
- [Hailee] Spurs.

00:03:03.529 --> 00:03:04.362
- Yep. Spurs.

00:03:04.362 --> 00:03:05.470
I use it as a pasta cutter.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.540
- [Kelly] Oh my God, you're
reminding me of a movie.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.373
I don't know if you've seen it.

00:03:08.373 --> 00:03:09.206
City Slickers?
- [Jamie] Yes.

00:03:09.206 --> 00:03:10.039
- With Billy Crystal?
- Yep.

00:03:10.039 --> 00:03:11.550
- That's who you're
reminding me of that movie.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.383
It's amazing.

00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:13.710
Well, your house is incredible!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.543
This is not a lie,

00:03:14.543 --> 00:03:16.290
I literally just told
my executive producer.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.160
I was reading about you and I,

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.830
look, I saw this and I was like,

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.410
oh my gosh, I want to build a house.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.400
- Do you want to come around for dinner?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.540
- [Kelly] Look at your house!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.828
Like, so you've been renovating it?

00:03:27.828 --> 00:03:29.738
- [Jamie] Yeah, it's a bit different now.

00:03:29.738 --> 00:03:30.571
- [Kelly] You inspired me.

00:03:30.571 --> 00:03:31.680
Last night. I started just,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.513
I want to build a house.

00:03:32.513 --> 00:03:33.780
And I want to make it look old like that.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.900
- Look, it's like a thousand years old.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.733
It's very old!
- [Kelly] I know!

00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:37.900
That's what I'm saying, it's beautiful!

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.940
- I try to, because Harry
Potter is the only person

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:40.820
that's sold more books than me,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.560
I thought I'd go and get Hogwarts.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.055
- [Kelly] Exactly. Exactly.

00:03:44.055 --> 00:03:45.390
- [Jamie] And you know,
do some dinner parties.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.994
- [Kelly] Build a moat
with some boats, yeah.

00:03:46.994 --> 00:03:48.407
- Exactly, there actually is a moat.

00:03:48.407 --> 00:03:49.240
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.073
- There is a moat!

00:03:50.073 --> 00:03:51.130
- [Kelly] Shut up! I want
to come to your house.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.323
- You can! It's an open house.

00:03:53.323 --> 00:03:55.920
- Oh my, I hear that's what you're trying

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.120
to do through, right? You and you're wife?

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.320
I heard that y'all were trying to like,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.890
almost make it open to
the public eventually?

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:00.723
- [Jamie] A part of it, yeah.

00:04:00.723 --> 00:04:03.010
We want to build a
restaurant, and a bakery,

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.950
and a cookery school.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:05.783
And yeah.

00:04:05.783 --> 00:04:06.653
(Audience cheers)

00:04:06.653 --> 00:04:07.880
- That's so cool!

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:12.880
- Yeah, well I mean, it's,
it's not that glamorous, right?

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.510
It's, you'd have to be mad
to buy something like that.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.570
- [Kelly] It's beautiful!

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.403
- And you have,

00:04:17.403 --> 00:04:19.290
I think for the people
that do try and keep these

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:21.690
places going, you've got
to have jobs for them.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.090
And I feel like I work for it.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.656
Like I don't own it. It owns me, so.

00:04:26.656 --> 00:04:28.075
- [Kelly] Anything,
anything old, you're always

00:04:28.075 --> 00:04:28.908
kind of redoing it.

00:04:28.908 --> 00:04:29.980
- Yeah, but I think it's
really important to give

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.897
buildings like that purpose and,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.540
and I want people to come
through it and experience it.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.820
So growing, cooking, baking, pickling,

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.554
smoking, proper hippie stuff.

00:04:40.554 --> 00:04:41.387
Come see me!

00:04:41.387 --> 00:04:42.620
- [Kelly] I love it!

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.453
- Yeah.

00:04:43.453 --> 00:04:45.166
- [Kelly] We get the hippy
thing with the names.

00:04:45.166 --> 00:04:47.390
So my thing is, I love
too, it's so English,

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.890
it reminds me of like Jane Austin novels,

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.780
when people used to go
tour other people's houses,

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.613
like in the novels.

00:04:51.613 --> 00:04:52.820
I just think it's the coolest idea,

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.050
and I really want you to
open this just so I can come.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:55.883
- You are welcome.

00:04:55.883 --> 00:04:57.837
- And we will, we will work
together, and write a song there

00:04:57.837 --> 00:04:58.670
and it will be the greatest song ever.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:04:59.503
- [Jamie] We have a recording
studio there as well.

00:04:59.503 --> 00:05:00.336
- You're not, do you really?

00:05:00.336 --> 00:05:02.460
- Honestly, if you ever
want to come record stuff,

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.020
- You have a recording studio there?

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:04.853
- Yeah!

00:05:04.853 --> 00:05:08.598
- Oh my Gosh! I was just
being funny about us going,

00:05:08.598 --> 00:05:09.480
I was just kidding.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:10.313
- It's happening now!

00:05:10.313 --> 00:05:11.146
- No, no! Just come,

00:05:11.146 --> 00:05:13.670
- [Kelly] That's very
Robbie Williams of you.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:14.503
- Today.

00:05:14.503 --> 00:05:15.745
No, but I will give you better food.

00:05:15.745 --> 00:05:17.180
- [Kelly] Okay! (laughs)

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.620
- [Jamie] Literally, you
can be sitting there.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.830
I've got the workflow going,
get your lyrics going.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:21.810
Look at the flowers,

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.310
I'll come in with canapes.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.143
It's going to be great!

00:05:24.143 --> 00:05:26.084
- [Hailee] I mean, let's go!

